<title>FINLAND: IVO and Tomen buy Hungarian power company.</title>
<headline>IVO and Tomen buy Hungarian power company.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish state-owned power producer Imatran Voima (IVO) said on Wednesday it had bought together with Japanese trading house Tomen Corporation a 73.7 percent stake in Hungarian  Budapest Eromu Rt power company.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the shares sold by the Hungarian privatisation agency is about 240 million markka ($47.7 million), half of which is IVO's stake,&quot; IVO said in a statement. ($ = 5.028 Finnish Markka)</p>
</text>
